Fixed. The state-aware branch (and the sibling `prByNumber` / `checkRunsByNumber` binary-expr growth from the same PR) is extracted out of `fixture` into named helpers at the top of `js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js`:

```javascript
function listPayload(opts, pr, state) {
    if (opts.prIndex) return JSON.stringify(opts.prIndex[state || 'open'] || []);
    return JSON.stringify([{ number: pr.number }]);
}
```

`fixture` is back at **12.0** (baseline 12) — verified with the pinned crap4js + released baseline + instrumented coverage: `0 regression(s), 0 new over threshold`. One subtlety: `a && a.state`-style arg guards inside the mock one-liners each count as a decision point on the enclosing function, so the helpers take the raw arg (undefined-safe by construction). Full suite: `run_mergeBot` 41/0, `run_machineSmAgent` 37/0, `run_smAgent` 552/0.

Fixed, TDD-style. Added a failing test first — `gh-952 > a WRAPPED merged-list payload ({ pullRequests: [...] }) still releases the slot (action() shape parity)` — which reproduced the exact silent-no-release you described (no release line, queue deferred with `acted: 0`, only the self-tick fired). Then normalized in `js/sm/mergeBot.js` by extracting the shape handling both consumers share:

```javascript
function listArray(prs) {
    return Array.isArray(prs) ? prs : (prs.pullRequests || prs.items || []);
}
```

`mergedSlotHolder` (line ~229) and `action()` (line ~315) both go through `listArray` now — same tool, same normalization, and a wrapped payload can no longer disable the release invisibly. Test is green; `run_mergeBot` 41/0.

